<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Radiokomunikace H1 1997 profit up.</title>
<headline>Czech Radiokomunikace H1 1997 profit up.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for six months ending June 30, 1997, according to Czech accounting standards: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Gross profit		   156.55     vs	   88.58</p>
<p> Operating profit	     180.98     vs	  114.69</p>
<p>Sales of own</p>
<p> goods and services	   809.64     vs	  663.64</p>
<p> Write-offs		     224.02     vs	  203.74</p>
<p> Basic capital		2,261.70     vs	2,259.52</p>
<p> Total assets		 3,891.92     vs	3,644.50</p>
<p>NOTE. Full company name is Ceske Radiokomunikace a.s., the former state microwave transmission firm. It holds a 51 percent stake in Radiomobil a.s., a digital mobile phone operator managed by Deutsche Telekcom unit DeTeMobil which leads a consortium hoding a 49 percent stake.</p>
<p>The Czech governmment holds a 69 percent stake in Radiokomunikace.</p>
<p>The results were provided by the company itself.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
